---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../site.config';

/**
 * Every statement on this page was verified against the built output before it
 * was written, not assumed:
 *   - no analytics or tracking script is present in dist/
 *   - no page loads any external script, stylesheet, image or iframe
 *   - document.cookie is never written
 *   - the only client storage is one localStorage key, `theme`
 *   - the only third-party request at runtime is OpenStreetMap tiles, on /map
 * If any of that changes, this page has to change with it.
 */
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy — Mission Sikhism"
  description="What this site collects: almost nothing. No cookies, no analytics, no tracking. Written plainly, and checked against the code."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container about">
      <span class="kicker">The short version</span>
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        This site sets no cookies, runs no analytics, and has no advertising,
        no accounts and no login. It does not know who you are, and it is not
        built to find out.
      </p>

      <p>
        Most privacy policies are long because the site has a lot to disclose.
        This one is short for the opposite reason, and everything below was
        checked against the actual build rather than described from intention.
      </p>

      <h2>No cookies, and therefore no cookie banner</h2>
      <p>
        The site never writes a cookie. That is why you were not asked to
        accept any — a consent banner for cookies that do not exist would be
        theatre, and an irritating piece of it.
      </p>

      <h2>The one thing stored on your device</h2>
      <p>
        If you use the light/dark toggle, your choice is saved in your
        browser's <em>local storage</em> under a single key named
        <code>theme</code>. It holds one word: <code>light</code> or
        <code>dark</code>.
      </p>
      <p>
        It never leaves your device and is never sent to us or to anyone else.
        Clearing your browser storage removes it, and the site then follows
        whatever your operating system prefers.
      </p>

      <h2>No analytics and no tracking</h2>
      <p>
        There is no Google Analytics, no tag manager, no pixel, no heatmap
        recorder and no advertising network. No page on this site loads any
        external script, stylesheet, font or image. Nothing follows you here
        and nothing follows you away.
      </p>

      <h2>Search runs on your own machine</h2>
      <p>
        The search on this site is built into the pages themselves. When you
        type a query it is matched against an index your browser has already
        downloaded — the words you search for are not transmitted anywhere and
        we could not read them if we wanted to.
      </p>

      <h2>The map is the one exception</h2>
      <p>
        The <a href="/map">Global Map</a> draws its background map from
        <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">OpenStreetMap</a>,
        a non-profit mapping project. Loading those tiles means your IP address
        and the area of the map you are looking at are visible to
        OpenStreetMap's servers, under
        <a href="https://osmfoundation.org/wiki/Privacy_Policy" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">their privacy policy</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        This happens only on the map page. Every other page on the site is
        served entirely from this domain. We flag it because it is the single
        place where visiting this site tells a third party anything at all.
      </p>

      <h2>Hosting</h2>
      <p>
        The site is static files served by Cloudflare Pages. Like any web host,
        Cloudflare processes the network requests needed to deliver a page and
        keeps operational logs for security and abuse prevention. We do not
        have access to visitor-level analytics from it, and we do not use it to
        build any profile of readers.
      </p>

      <h2>If you email us</h2>
      <p>
        The correction and suggestion links on this site open your own mail
        client addressed to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
        Nothing is submitted through the site — there is no form, and no data
        reaches us unless you choose to send it.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you do write, we hold your message and address for as long as it
        takes to deal with it and to credit a contribution. We do not add you
        to any list, because there isn't one. Ask us to delete your
        correspondence and we will.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        The site is suitable for all ages and collects nothing from anyone,
        which includes children.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Data protection law — the UK and EU GDPR among others — gives you
        rights to access, correct and erase personal data held about you. We
        hold none, unless you have emailed us, in which case it is the email
        you sent. Write to the address above to exercise any of this.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If the site ever starts collecting something, this page changes first
        and says so plainly. Its history is public in the repository, so you
        can see exactly what it said before.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
